hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1151","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""O Muslim women! Let not any neighbor look down upon (even) the gift of another neighbor, even if it is the meat of a sheep's foot."""
"1152","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said to Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him): ""O my nephew! Indeed, we would see one crescent, then see the next crescent, and in this way, in two months, we would see three crescents (i.e., two full months would pass), and no fire would be lit in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" (That is, no food would be cooked.) Urwah says: I asked, ""O Aunt! Then how did you live?"" She replied, ""On two things: by eating dates and drinking water. However, yes, some Ansar lived near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and they had some milk animals, and they would send their milk (as a gift) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he would also give us to drink from it."""
"1153","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""If I am invited to eat the meat of a foreleg or thigh, I will surely go, and if a foreleg or thigh of meat is sent to me as a gift (i.e., as a present), I will also accept it."""
"1154","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we drove a rabbit out from its place at the location of Mar al-Zahran, then people ran after it but they became tired, and I managed to overpower it and caught it. Then I brought it to Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him), he slaughtered it and sent its back or thighs to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) accepted it. In another narration, it is mentioned that he (peace and blessings be upon him) ate from it."
"1155","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that his maternal aunt Umm Hufaid sent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift of cheese, ghee, and sahna (a kind of animal). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate the cheese and ghee, but left the sahna with aversion. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""But the sahna was eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). If it had been forbidden, how could it have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"""
"1156","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Whenever any food was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would ask about it: ""Is it a gift or charity?"" If it was said that it was charity, he (peace be upon him) would say to his companions (may Allah be pleased with them): ""You eat,"" and he himself would not eat from it. But if it was said that it was a gift, he (peace be upon him) would extend his hand and eat with them."
"1157","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that meat was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was mentioned that this was given to Barirah (may Allah be pleased with her) as charity. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is charity for her and a gift for us."""
"1158","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that among the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) there were two groups: one group included Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha, Hafsa, Safiyya, and Sawda (may Allah be pleased with them), and the other group included Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) and the rest of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Muslims knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) loved Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (the truthful, pure, and chaste) the most. So, when any of them had a gift and wanted to give it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), they would hold it back until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in the house of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and then the one bringing the gift would deliver it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at the house of Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha. At this, the group of Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) discussed the matter and said to Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her): “Ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to tell whoever wants to give him a gift to do so wherever he may be among his wives.” So Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) conveyed what the other wives had said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but he did not reply to her. Then the wives asked Umm Salama if she had received a reply, and she said, “I did not get any reply.” The wives said to her, “Ask him again.” When her turn came again, she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), but again he did not reply. The wives asked her again, “Did you get any reply?” She said, “He did not give me any reply.” Then the wives said, “Ask him again so that he may reply to you.” So when her turn came, she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: “Do not trouble me regarding Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), for by Allah, no revelation comes to me in the garment of any wife except Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her).” Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) said, “O Messenger of Allah! I seek forgiveness from Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for causing you any distress.” After that, the wives called Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her), the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and sent her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to say: “Your wives ask you, by Allah, to be just concerning the daughter of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him).” So she conveyed this to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O my daughter! Do you not love what I love?” She said, “Yes, indeed, I love what you love.” So Sayyida Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) returned to the wives and told them what had happened. The wives said to her, “Go again to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him),” but she refused to go again. Then the wives sent Umm al-Mu’minin Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her), who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and spoke harshly, saying: “Your wives ask you, by Allah, to be just concerning the daughter of Ibn Abi Quhafah (i.e., Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her),” and she raised her voice until she spoke harshly to Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) in her presence. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) to see if she would respond. (The narrator says) Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) began to reply to her until she silenced Umm al-Mu’minin Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: “Why not! She is the daughter of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him).”"
"1159","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not refuse perfume."
"1160","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to accept gifts and would give something in return."
"1161","Narrated from Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he says: My father gave me something, so (my mother) Amrah bint Rawahah said that I am not pleased until you make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a witness to this. So he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and submitted: I have given something to my son who is from Amrah bint Rawahah, but Amrah (my wife) said that I should make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a witness to it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: “Have you given the same to all your sons?” He replied: No. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Fear Allah and be just among your children.” (Nu’man, may Allah be pleased with him, says that) then he took back what he had given."
"1162","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that vomits and then eats its vomit."""
"1163","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Maimunah bint Al-Harith (may Allah be pleased with her) that she freed one of her slave girls without seeking permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then, when it was her turn (the day when the Prophet would stay with her), she said, ""Do you know that I have freed my slave girl?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Have you really freed her?"" She replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""If you had given her to your maternal relatives, you would have obtained more reward in that."""
"1164","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Whosever name was drawn, he would take her with him. And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would assign one day and night for each of his wives, except for Sawda bint Zam’a (may Allah be pleased with her), who gave her day and night to Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), seeking thereby the pleasure of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1165","Sayyiduna Miswar bin Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed some cloaks and did not give any to Sayyiduna Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said, ""O my son! Take me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" So I went with him. Then he said, ""Go inside and call the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on my behalf."" He says that I called you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so you came out and one of those cloaks was with you. You (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This we have kept for you."" When he saw it, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Is Makhramah pleased or not?"""
"1166","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the house of Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her), but he did not enter it (he returned from outside). When Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came, Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him about it. He then asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding this matter, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw a silk curtain at the door."" (That is why I returned.) He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What do we have to do with the world?"" Then he went back to the house and informed them of this. Sayyidah Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) said that whatever you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command regarding it (that will be done). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Give this curtain to such-and-such needy people."""
"1167","Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me a striped silk garment, and I wore it. Then I saw the effect of anger on the blessed face of the Prophet (peace be upon him), so I tore it and distributed it among my (female) relatives."
"1168","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were one hundred and thirty men with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""Does anyone among you have any food?"" Then a person had about one sa’ of grain, etc., which was kneaded. After that, a tall, disheveled-haired polytheist came, driving his goats. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Are these for sale or a gift from someone?"" Or the Prophet (peace be upon him) used the word ""hiba"" instead of ""gift."" He said, ""No, rather they are for sale."" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) bought a goat from him, then it was slaughtered, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered that the liver, etc., be roasted. By Allah, there was not a single person among the one hundred and thirty men to whom the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not give pieces of liver. Whoever was present, he gave to him, and whoever was not present, he set aside for him. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) placed the meat of the goat in two large trays, so all the people ate and we were all satisfied, and still, whatever was left in the trays, we put it on the camel, or he said something similar."
"1169","Lady Asma bint Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with her) says that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my mother came to me and she was a polytheist. (I neither allowed her to enter the house nor accepted her gift.) After that, I sought a verdict from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I also said that my mother has come to me with affection, so should I treat my mother well? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes, treat your mother well."""
"1170","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that (during the days when Marwan was the ruler, in a certain case) he testified that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had given these two houses and the chamber to Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him). So Marwan, based on his testimony, ruled in favor of the daughters of Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1171","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the verdict regarding ‘Umra that it belongs to the one to whom it was gifted."
"1172","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that Umm Ayman (may Allah be pleased with her) came to her wearing a thick shirt, the price of which would have been five dirhams. So she (Aisha) said, ""Look at my maid, she acts proud wearing this shirt at home, and during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), I had a similar shirt, and whenever any woman in Madinah was to be adorned, she would borrow that shirt from me."""
"1173","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when the Muhajirun migrated from Makkah to Madinah, they had nothing with them, while the Ansar possessed land and wealth. The Ansar distributed their wealth among the Muhajirun on the condition that every year the Muhajirun would give them half of the fruit, and all the labor from beginning to end would be done by them. And his mother, that is, the mother of Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), Umm Sulaym, who was also the mother of Abdullah bin Abi Talhah, gave a few date trees to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave those trees to his freed slave woman, Umm Ayman, who was the mother of Usamah bin Zayd. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the Battle of Khaybar and returned to Madinah, the Muhajirun returned the things that had been given to them, that is, the orchards and trees which the Ansar had given to the Muhajirun. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also returned the trees to the mother of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and in exchange, he gave Umm Ayman some trees from his own garden."
"1174","Narrated Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are forty good qualities, the best of which is lending a she-goat. Whoever acts upon any of these qualities, hoping for reward and believing in Allah's promise, Allah will admit him to Paradise."""
